---
import ReferencePage from "../layouts/ReferencePage.astro";
import {LINKS, RELEASE} from "../site.ts";
import {FAILURE_SOURCES} from "../failure-handling.ts";
const root=`${LINKS.github}/blob/v${RELEASE}/docs`;
const guides=[
["Start with a live channel","getting-started.md","Scaffold a fixture project, open the local workbench, and subscribe from a browser."],
["Add StreamOtter to your app","existing-app.md","Connect your identity, handlers, and authoritative state to an existing application."],
["Connect to Kafka","kafka.md","Configure a broker connection and move from fixture records to a Kafka source."],
["Troubleshoot a view","troubleshooting.md","Follow state changes, source health, and errors to the part that needs attention."],
["Handle bad records","source-failures.md","Turn on source-failure policies, write an honest recovery guard, and operate incidents from the CLI."]];
---
<ReferencePage title="Build with StreamOtter" description="A map to the maintained guides and reference, pinned to the release this site runs.">
  <section class="reference-grid" aria-label="Guides">{guides.map(([title,path,copy])=><article class="reference-card"><h2><a href={`${root}/guides/${path}`}>{title} ↗</a></h2><p>{copy}</p></article>)}</section>
  <section aria-labelledby="api-reference"><h2 id="api-reference">API reference</h2><p><a href="/docs/api/">Every export of streamotter@{RELEASE}</a>: the browser SDK, the gateway, the shared contracts, the operator and management APIs, and the CLI. It is generated from the declarations and doc comments in the published package when this site is built, so it always matches the release the site runs.</p></section>
  <section><h2>Specifications and release</h2><ul><li><a href={`${root}/V1_API.md`}>V1 API specification: contracts, handlers, SDK, states, and protocol</a></li><li><a href={FAILURE_SOURCES.api}>V1.1 API: failureHandling, recovery guards, incidents, and the operator service</a></li><li><a href={FAILURE_SOURCES.spec}>V1.1 source-failure specification</a> and its <a href={FAILURE_SOURCES.decisions}>decision records</a></li><li><a href={LINKS.status}>Implementation status and verified support matrix</a></li><li><a href={LINKS.changelog}>Changelog</a></li><li><a href={`${LINKS.npm}/v/${RELEASE}`}>streamotter@{RELEASE} on npm</a></li></ul><p>The guides and specifications open the library’s own documentation on GitHub or npm, pinned to this release. The site does not maintain a second copy.</p></section>
  <section aria-labelledby="site-docs"><h2 id="site-docs">On this site</h2><ul><li><a href="/when-it-breaks/#source-failure-policies">The source-failure policies and record disposition, summarized</a></li><li><a href={`${LINKS.demoRepo}/blob/main/docs/LOCAL_LAB.md`}>Run the Failure Lab locally ↗</a>: the Kafka stack with three isolated benches.</li></ul></section>
</ReferencePage>
